  "formula": {
    "tex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\term{coefficients}{b}&=\\term{moments}{S_{xx}}^{-1}s_{xy},\n&\\term{intercept}{b_0}&=\\bar y-\\sum_j b_j\\bar x_j\\\\\n\\term{sigmaSquared}{\\hat\\sigma^2}&=\\frac{\\term{residualSumSquares}{\\mathrm{RSS}}}{\\term{freedom}{n-p}},\n&\\term{standardErrors}{\\mathrm{se}_j}&=\\sqrt{\\hat\\sigma^2\\,[S_{xx}^{-1}]_{jj}}\\\\\n\\term{tStatistics}{t_j}&=\\frac{b_j}{\\mathrm{se}_j},\n&\\term{rSquared}{R^2}&=1-\\frac{\\mathrm{RSS}}{\\term{totalSumSquares}{\\mathrm{TSS}}}\n\\end{aligned}",
    "ascii": "b = Sxx^-1 sxy; b0 = ybar - sum_j b_j xbar_j; sigma2 = RSS/(n-p); se_j = sqrt(sigma2 [Sxx^-1]_jj); t_j = b_j/se_j; R2 = 1 - RSS/TSS. S are centred cross-products of the finite rows; the unit-scaled normal equations are solved by Cholesky, optionally with ridge lambda added to the predictor diagonal. p counts the intercept; the intercept variance is sigma2 (1/n + xbar Sxx^-1 xbar).",
